---
import Layout from '../../smarttec-investor/components/Layout.astro';
import Journey from '../../smarttec-investor/components/Journey.astro';
import InvestorDeck from '../../smarttec-investor/components/InvestorDeck.astro';
import Underwriting from '../../smarttec-investor/components/Underwriting.astro';
import {investmentReadiness as readiness} from '../../smarttec-investor/investment-readiness.mjs';
import CinematicArt from '../../components/CinematicArt.astro';
import '../../styles/cinematic-investor.css';
import BrandLockup from '../../components/BrandLockup.astro';
import {pageAccess,privateHeaders} from '../../smarttec-investor/server/auth.mjs';
import campus from '../../smarttec-investor/data/campus.json';
import ArchitecturalCampus from '../../smarttec-architecture/ArchitecturalCampus.astro';
export const prerender=false;
Object.entries(privateHeaders).forEach(([k,v])=>Astro.response.headers.set(k,v));
const access=await pageAccess(Astro.request);
if(access.error) return new Response('Private access is temporarily unavailable.',{status:503,headers:privateHeaders});
if(!access.session) return Astro.redirect('/investors/login',303);
const usd=(value:number)=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:0}).format(value);
---
<Layout>
<a href="#opportunity" class="inv-skip">Skip to content</a>
<Journey />
<main id="inv-main">
<section id="opportunity" class="inv-hero inv-section">
  <CinematicArt path="/investors" instance="investment" />
  <div class="inv-hero-copy">
    <p class="inv-eyebrow">MEAD, OKLAHOMA / DEVELOPMENT STAGE</p>
    <h1>Build the first revenue.<br/><em>Earn the next expansion.</em></h1>
    <div class="inv-actions" aria-label="Investor presentations"><a href="/investors/pitch" class="inv-button" data-pitch-launch>Open immersive investor deck <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/api/investor/presentation" class="inv-outline" download="SmartTec-Investor-Presentation.pdf">Download investor PDF</a></div>
    <p class="inv-lead">A proposed {readiness.hardware.installedGPUs}-B300 deployment on a 39.39-acre campus. Founder funding, long-term site access and a behind-the-meter power strategy support the plan. Customer contracts and complete installed costs are the next milestones.</p>
    <nav class="inv-hero-links" aria-label="Explore the investor plan"><a href="#deployment">Explore the deployment ↓</a><a href="#capital">Review the capital plan ↓</a></nav>
  </div>
  <div class="inv-hero-bottom"><span>8460 US 70, Mead, OK 73449<br/><small>AI CONCEPT / NOT A SURVEYED SITE PLAN</small></span><span>PROPOSED FIRST DEPLOYMENT<br/><strong>{readiness.hardware.systems} systems / {readiness.hardware.installedGPUs} B300 GPUs</strong></span></div>
</section>
<InvestorDeck />
<ArchitecturalCampus />
<section id="site-map" class="inv-section inv-light"><p class="inv-eyebrow">01 / THE CAMPUS</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>One property.<br/>Three development areas.</h2><p>The 39.39-acre legal parcel extends south from US 70. The map preserves the earlier survey traces and proposed development areas.</p></div><div class="inv-map-shell"><div class="inv-map-tools"><button id="inv-map-plan">3D site plan</button><button id="inv-map-satellite">Satellite</button><button id="inv-map-tilt">Toggle 2D / 3D</button><button id="inv-map-reset">Full campus</button></div><p id="inv-map-status" role="status">Loading interactive concept plan…</p><div id="inv-campus-map" aria-label="Interactive campus concept map"></div><div id="inv-map-layers" class="inv-map-tools"></div><div id="inv-map-features" class="inv-map-tools"></div><p id="inv-map-detail" aria-live="polite">Choose a building or development area for details.</p><details class="inv-details"><summary>Satellite alignment / designer controls</summary><p>Satellite imagery is dated photography. The default address anchor is approximate. Enter longitude, latitude for the northwest, northeast and southwest property corners to preview alignment. Visual alignment is not survey verification. Changes last only in this browser session; download the registration for your designer.</p><form id="inv-map-align"><label>Northwest <input name="northWest" required aria-label="Northwest longitude comma latitude"/></label><label>Northeast <input name="northEast" required aria-label="Northeast longitude comma latitude"/></label><label>Southwest <input name="southWest" required aria-label="Southwest longitude comma latitude"/></label><button type="submit">Preview alignment</button><button id="inv-map-download" type="button">Download registration</button></form></details><p class="inv-note">Concept massing: footprint positions, orientation and heights are illustrative. Written factory dimensions control over the size of the red annotation boxes. No engineering approval is implied.</p><a class="inv-outline inv-dark-outline" href="/api/investor/marked-survey">Download your marked layout</a></div><div class="inv-campus-grid"><div><p class="inv-big">{campus.totalAcres} <span>acres</span></p><p>Current legal parcel area supplied by the owner. Earlier survey tract annotations total 39.21 acres; their original geometry and labels are retained below.</p><p class="inv-note">Legal description: {campus.legalDescription}</p><div class="inv-tract-list">{campus.tracts.map(t=><button class="inv-tract" data-tract={t.id}><span>TRACT {t.id} / {t.acres.toFixed(2)} AC</span><strong>{t.status}</strong><small>{t.description}</small></button>)}</div><p class="inv-note">A (1,500 sq ft) and C (3,535 sq ft) provide 5,035 sq ft of gross data-center area. B (2,083 sq ft) serves utility, battery and storage uses. Marks 1 (east), 2 (middle) and 3 (west) correspond to A, B and C. B and the separate house/office are excluded from data-center area.</p><a class="inv-outline inv-dark-outline" href="/api/investor/survey">Download supplied survey</a><p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8460%20US%2070%2C%20Mead%2C%20OK%2073449" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open address in maps</a></p></div><div><div class="inv-survey-toolbar"><button data-survey="all">Full site</button><button data-survey="in">Zoom +</button><button data-survey="out">Zoom −</button></div><div class="inv-survey" id="inv-survey"><img id="inv-survey-image" src="/api/investor/survey-image" alt="Supplied BM Surveying boundary plat showing US 70 at the north, three tracts and existing structures"/></div><p class="inv-note">BM Surveying plat dated 28 December 2025. Pan to inspect; use the original document for dimensions. Screen zoom is not a survey scale.</p></div></div><details class="inv-details"><summary>Survey notes and development limits</summary><p>{campus.easements}</p><ul>{campus.limitations.map(n=><li>{n}</li>)}</ul><p>Tract 2: 495-foot depth in its legal description. Tract 3: 1,200-foot depth. New factory footprints and solar layouts are proposed and are not approved by this boundary survey.</p></details></section>
<section id="deployment" class="inv-section">
  <p class="inv-eyebrow">02 / THE PROPOSED FIRST DEPLOYMENT</p>
  <div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>A focused B300 fleet.<br/>One building to commission.</h2><p>Management proposes {readiness.hardware.systems} complete liquid-cooled {readiness.hardware.supplier} systems in one existing building. At the owner-reported {usd(readiness.hardware.systemPrice)} per eight-GPU system, hardware alone totals {usd(readiness.hardware.totalCost)}. This is the current planning scope, pending procurement and acceptance.</p></div>
  <div class="inv-stat-row"><div><strong>{readiness.hardware.systems}</strong><span>Complete systems proposed</span></div><div><strong>{readiness.hardware.installedGPUs}</strong><span>B300 GPUs in the purchase plan</span></div><div><strong>{readiness.hardware.saleableGPUs}</strong><span>Saleable GPUs modeled</span></div><div><strong>{readiness.hardware.reserveGPUs}</strong><span>Financial reserve GPUs</span></div></div>
  <p class="inv-note">{readiness.hardware.reserveNote} The owner identifies Supermicro and describes a complete system including CPUs, NVSwitch, networking, storage, NVIDIA software and support. Exact configuration, service duration and external cluster scope remain to be reconciled.</p>
  <div class="inv-three-col"><article><span>01</span><h3>Contract the workload</h3><p>Active customer discussions are under way. No signed customer contract or paid pilot is established. Agree GPU quantity, workload acceptance, net pricing, minimum payments and start dates.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Price the complete installation</h3><p>The selected building needs entirely new cooling. Mechanical, electrical and plumbing contractors can compare a simpler plant, new or warranted refurbished equipment, and complete installation scopes.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Commission, then expand</h3><p>Verify usable power, fiber, temperatures, failover and customer performance before service acceptance. Expansion beyond the first fleet needs its own customer commitments and costed plan.</p></article></div>
  <details class="inv-details"><summary>How the current plan relates to earlier concepts</summary><p>The earlier two-RTX/one-B300 starter mix and previous fleet-size studies remain available as historical calculator examples. They do not describe today's proposed first deployment or establish its updated return.</p></details>
</section>
<section id="capital" class="inv-section inv-light">
  <p class="inv-eyebrow">03 / FOUNDER FUNDING AND CAPITAL USE</p>
  <div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Fund the first phase.<br/>Price the remaining scope.</h2><p>Management reports {usd(readiness.founderCapital.initialAvailable)} available initially and willingness to personally fund the overage. The additional amount, timing and contribution terms remain to be documented. A fixed outside-investor raise has not been established.</p></div>
  <div class="inv-three-col"><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">INITIAL FOUNDER CAPITAL</p><h3 class="inv-number">${(readiness.founderCapital.initialAvailable/1e6).toFixed(0)}m</h3><p>Owner-reported available funds, with willingness to cover additional project costs. Funding availability and transfers have not been independently verified.</p></article><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">PROPOSED GPU HARDWARE</p><h3 class="inv-number">${(readiness.hardware.totalCost/1e6).toFixed(2)}m</h3><p>{readiness.hardware.systems} complete {readiness.hardware.supplier} eight-B300 systems at {usd(readiness.hardware.systemPrice)} each, based on the owner's price. Cooling and remaining site work need separate scope reconciliation.</p></article><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">REPORTED SITE AGREEMENT</p><h3 class="inv-number">{readiness.property.siteAgreementYears} years</h3><p>Management confirms both parties signed an agreement with BC LLC, the related-party landholder. The site is reported paid off. This establishes neither SmartTec ownership of the land nor investor collateral.</p></article></div>
  <div class="inv-current-budget">
    <h3>Two cooling comparisons. A complete project total is still open.</h3>
    <p>Both columns below retain {usd(readiness.budget.startupAllowance)} of earlier startup/acquisition allowances and a {usd(readiness.budget.openingReserve)} opening reserve. These amounts require review for overlaps and updated operating costs.</p>
    <div class="inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Partial initial funding comparisons; scroll horizontally on small screens">
      <table><caption>Partial initial budget in USD. Excludes unknown non-cooling site work, reserve revisions and later cash calls.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Planning comparison</th><th scope="col">Installed cooling allowance</th><th scope="col">Partial initial funding</th><th scope="col">Additional founder funds above $6m</th></tr></thead><tbody>{readiness.cooling.cases.map(item=><tr><th scope="row">{item.label}</th><td data-label="Cooling allowance">{usd(item.installedCoolingAllowance)}</td><td data-label="Partial initial funding">{usd(item.partialInitialFunding)}</td><td data-label="Additional founder funds">{usd(item.additionalFounderContribution)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    </div>
    <p class="inv-note">{readiness.cooling.cases[0].basis}</p>
    <p class="inv-note">{readiness.cooling.cases[1].basis} The building has no existing air conditioning, so complete new room or rack-air cooling remains in scope.</p>
    <p><strong>Complete funding and updated ROI are not yet established.</strong> Replace the previous {usd(readiness.budget.oldCombinedSiteAllowance)} combined site allowance with separately priced cooling and non-cooling work. Reconcile taxes, freight, installation and service coverage before removing any overlap.</p>
  </div>
  <details class="inv-details"><summary>Site agreement and capital-release milestones</summary><p>BC LLC is associated with the CEO. Management describes an annual payment of 1% of profit remaining after expenses. The signed agreement and its accounting definition have not been reviewed; that payment is not yet included in the calculator. Related-party obligations, site rights, investor rights and contribution terms need to be resolved together.</p><ol><li>Define customer payment obligations and acceptance requirements.</li><li>Reconcile complete supplier and contractor prices, firm power and network delivery.</li><li>Document founder contributions, site-use rights and any external investment terms.</li><li>Complete commissioning and demonstrate collected receipts before expansion.</li></ol><p>Manufacturing buildings, expanded compute, solar and storage development have separate budgets. The earlier construction and service dates remain management targets, subject to delivery readiness.</p></details>
</section>
<section id="returns" class="inv-section inv-machine"><p class="inv-eyebrow">04 / RETURNS EXPLORER</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>What has to be true<br/>for this to work?</h2><p>The updated project return remains open while costs and commercial terms are reconciled. Use the historical examples or your own complete inputs to explore conditional cash flows; these results do not establish investor distributions.</p></div><Underwriting /><p id="inv-app-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading private scenario tools…</p><div id="inv-calculator" hidden><div class="inv-actions"><button id="inv-new" class="inv-outline">Build my scenario</button><button id="inv-example" class="inv-button">Load RTX-only illustration</button><label class="inv-outline inv-import">Import scenario JSON<input type="file" id="inv-import" accept="application/json,.json"/></label></div><div id="inv-illustration-note" class="inv-warning" hidden><strong>RTX-only hypothetical illustration — excludes B300.</strong><p>This earlier two-server example includes unverified network pricing and synthetic equipment costs. It is not a quote, forecast or budget for the current 64-B300 deployment. Every input remains editable.</p><details><summary>Read every illustration assumption</summary><ul id="inv-provenance"></ul></details></div><div id="inv-underwriting-note" class="inv-warning" hidden></div><form id="inv-scenario-form"><div class="inv-editor-heading"><h3>1. Equipment and customer revenue</h3><button type="button" id="inv-add-row" class="inv-outline">Add equipment</button></div><div id="inv-equipment-rows"></div><h3>2. Site, costs and funding</h3><div id="inv-global-fields" class="inv-fields"></div><details class="inv-details"><summary>Advanced cash timing, financing and exit assumptions</summary><div id="inv-advanced-fields" class="inv-fields"></div><label class="inv-check"><input id="inv-share-enabled" type="checkbox"/> Show a pro-rata investor illustration</label><div id="inv-share-field" hidden></div><h4>Later capital expenditure</h4><div id="inv-capex-events"></div><button type="button" class="inv-outline" id="inv-add-capex">Add capital cost event</button></details><label class="inv-check"><input id="inv-acknowledge" type="checkbox" required/> I understand these are conditional assumptions; hardware prices and usable site capacity require verification.</label><button type="submit" class="inv-button">Calculate this scenario</button></form><p class="inv-note">Pre-tax monthly cash model. Property, manufacturing, solar and storage returns are excluded. All entered equipment is purchased at time zero; contract expiry is explicit. A positive financial result does not establish available capacity.</p><section id="inv-results" hidden aria-label="Calculated scenario results"><div class="inv-editor-heading"><h3>Your conditional result</h3><span id="inv-result-basis"></span></div><div id="inv-result-cards" class="inv-result-cards"></div><div class="inv-chart-wrap"><h4>Cumulative project capital recovered</h4><svg id="inv-cash-chart" viewBox="0 0 800 250" role="img" aria-label="Cumulative monthly project cash flow"></svg><p class="inv-note">Includes the initial contribution, capital calls, distributions and terminal cash. Hovering is not required: the monthly table below provides exact values.</p></div><div class="inv-actions"><button id="inv-export-json" class="inv-outline">Download full scenario</button><button id="inv-export-csv" class="inv-outline">Download monthly ledger</button><button id="inv-print" class="inv-outline">Print investor summary</button><button id="inv-stress" class="inv-outline">Compare a downside case</button><button id="inv-matrix" class="inv-outline">Occupancy × price sensitivity</button><button id="inv-price-floor" class="inv-outline">Find required modeled price</button></div><div id="inv-sensitivity"></div><div id="inv-matrix-results"></div><div id="inv-price-result"></div><div id="inv-print-assumptions" class="inv-print-only"></div><details class="inv-details"><summary>Monthly cash-flow table</summary><div class="inv-table-scroll" id="inv-cash-table"></div></details></section></div></section>
<section id="evidence" class="inv-section inv-light">
  <p class="inv-eyebrow">05 / CURRENT EVIDENCE AND NEXT MILESTONES</p>
  <div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Make each commitment<br/>ready to underwrite.</h2><p>Management updates define the proposed first fleet and funding intent. Documents, contractor prices and acceptance tests must establish what can be delivered.</p></div>
  <div class="inv-evidence">
    <div><strong>Boundary survey</strong><span>Supplied historical document reviewed; current owner-reported legal area is 39.39 acres.</span><a href="/api/investor/survey">Download original copy</a></div>
    <div><strong>Founder capital</strong><span>$6m initially available and willingness to cover overage, owner-reported. Additional timing, legal form and transfers unverified.</span></div>
    <div><strong>BC LLC site agreement</strong><span>50-year agreement signed by both parties, owner-confirmed. Annual 1% after-expense profit description needs document and accounting review.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Customer demand</strong><span>Active discussions. No signed customer contract, paid pilot or binding minimum receipts established.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Hardware and cooling</strong><span>Eight complete Supermicro B300 systems proposed at $670,000 each, owner-reported. All cooling is new; final installed quotes and OEM compatibility remain open.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Power delivery</strong><span>Solar, batteries and gas supply agreement below 7¢/kWh reported. Firm exclusive continuous kW, full cost scope and operating date await the team. Utility commissioning target: 8 October 2026.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Dobson fiber delivery</strong><span>Not live. Management target 8 October–5 November 2026; carrier terms and route diversity require confirmation.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Issuer and investment rights</strong><span>Final raise, contribution structure and investor cash rights remain to be agreed.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p>Customer demand, collections, equipment life, infrastructure delivery and operating costs determine the return on all project capital. Founder funding does not itself establish profitability. Historical calculator results are not an updated investment forecast.</p>
</section>
<section id="questions" class="inv-section"><p class="inv-eyebrow">06 / QUESTIONS, WITH CONTEXT</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Ask the project records.</h2><p>Answers come from the supplied survey, owner statements and the documented financial method. Missing facts stay visible.</p></div><form id="inv-question-form" class="inv-question-form"><label for="inv-question">Your question</label><div class="inv-login-row"><input id="inv-question" placeholder="Is the property included in investor returns?" minlength="3" maxlength="1000" required/><button class="inv-button" type="submit">Find an answer</button></div></form><p class="inv-note">Curated knowledge search. This does not connect to private chat history or provide personalized investment advice.</p><div id="inv-answer" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="inv-faq-list"></div></section>
</main><footer class="inv-footer"><BrandLockup /><p>8460 US 70, Mead, OK 73449<br/>Development-stage project • Reviewed September 2026</p><a href="/contact">Request a technical discussion</a><p class="inv-note">Private planning information. Current funding and equipment figures include management statements and analyst estimates. Securities terms and the offering route remain to be established.</p></footer>
</Layout>
<script>import '../../smarttec-investor/client/app.mjs';</script>

<style>
  .inv-hero-copy [data-pitch-launch]{gap:14px}
  .inv-hero-links{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:12px 28px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:13px;color:#d0e7d8}
  .inv-hero-links a{text-underline-offset:4px}
  .inv-current-budget{margin:3rem 0;padding:clamp(1.1rem,3vw,2.25rem);border:1px solid #a7b9ad;background:#e8eee8;border-radius:1rem}
  .inv-current-budget h3{font-size:clamp(1.45rem,2.6vw,2.25rem);line-height:1.2;margin-top:0}
  .inv-current-budget table{width:100%;min-width:760px;border-collapse:collapse;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .inv-current-budget caption{text-align:left;padding:1rem 0;font-size:.9rem}
  .inv-current-budget .inv-table-scroll{max-height:none}
  .inv-current-budget th,.inv-current-budget td{text-align:left;padding:1rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid #b2c1b6;vertical-align:top}
  .inv-current-budget thead th{font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.4;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.03em}
  .inv-current-budget .inv-note{font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.6}
  @media(max-width:700px){.inv-current-budget table{min-width:0;display:block}.inv-current-budget caption{display:block}.inv-current-budget thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip-path:inset(50%)}.inv-current-budget tbody,.inv-current-budget tr{display:block}.inv-current-budget tbody tr{padding:1rem 0;border-top:1px solid #a7b9ad}.inv-current-budget th,.inv-current-budget td{display:block;border:0;padding:.5rem 0}.inv-current-budget td::before{content:attr(data-label);display:block;font-size:.75rem;color:#52655b;margin-bottom:.2rem}.inv-current-budget td{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600}}
</style>
